.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH scanr-output 1  "scanr-output " 
.SH NAME
scanr\-output \- Inspect prior scan records
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscanr\-output\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect prior scan records
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
scanr\-output\-summarize(1)
Summarize a scan record: totals, and counts by host, network, and service
.TP
scanr\-output\-verify(1)
Check a scan record for integrity and completeness
.TP
scanr\-output\-remainder(1)
Print targets that were not fully probed, for feeding back into \-\-targets
.TP
scanr\-output\-events(1)
Write the raw JSONL event stream, decompressing it if needed
.TP
scanr\-output\-results(1)
Every probe result, with spans expanded; filter by host, port, or state
.TP
scanr\-output\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
